A men's diamond engagement ring is not a women's ring scaled to a larger size. The design intent is different. Men's bands run 5–8mm wide vs 2–3mm for most women's engagement rings. That changes how the diamond element has to be sized, set, and proportioned.

Men's engagement rings are mainstream now. Same-sex couples led this trend first. It is now a common option for any groom who wants to wear a ring during the engagement period.

The certified market now reflects that shift. Blue Nile's inventory has 23 purpose-built men's diamond engagement ring designs — from the most restrained grooved solitaires to geometric hexagon diamond channel patterns. The range covers $1,000 to $4,575 (setting prices; channel set rings include diamond weight).

